//? Title: Shamos–Hoey detection: actual AVL events, exact neighbors and vertical contacts
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given many closed finite segments, decide whether any distinct pair intersects
and retain an original-identity witness. Actual native endpoint events and
neighbor tests precede the original disjoint, crossing and four-segment
examples.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Before the first intersection, the vertical order of active nonvertical segments
cannot exchange. A crossing pair must become neighbors before they cross; test
newly adjacent pairs on insertion and removal. Sort endpoint events, maintain
order in a balanced AVL tree and stop on the first witness. Each insertion
height comparison uses the incoming endpoint and an exact orientation of the
active segment, avoiding rounded division and a changing container comparator.
Same-x starts precede vertical interval queries and ends. A vertical interval
needs only the first active height at or above its lower endpoint; adjacent
lower-y-sorted verticals handle vertical overlap. Sorting and balanced searches
give O(n log n) bounded-word work and O(n) intrinsic storage; this detects one
witness rather than enumerating all crossings.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/shamos_hoey_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/shamos_hoey.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    namespace z = dm::geometry;
    auto r = z::shamos_hoey_trace({{{0, 0}, {2, 2}}, {{0, 2}, {2, 0}}});
    std::print("| actual tested first id | second id | exact contact |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &p : r.pairs)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", p.first, p.second, p.intersects);
    std::print("\nActual events processed {}, height tests {}.\n",
               r.events_processed, r.height_tests);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Two crossing closed segments");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual pair tests {}", r.pair_tests));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual witness {},{}", r.first, r.second));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/shamos_hoey_tiny.svg");
}
```
