> API and interpretation

Each witness names original caller segment identities. Complete pair predicates
use exact stored-coordinate signs and never construct rounded crossing
coordinates. Equal-x event phases include endpoint contacts; vertical segments
stay outside the nonvertical status. Selected counters exclude event-sort
comparisons and internals of the fixed exact determinant kernel. Optional
histories have independent actual-record caps.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Shamos and Hoey, Geometric Intersection Problems (1976)|https://euro.ecom.cmu.edu/people/faculty/mshamos/1976GeometricIntersection.pdf]

